{{also|morgen}}
==German==

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈmɔrɡən/|[ˈmɔʁ-]|[ˈmɔɐ̯-]|[ˈmɔː-]|[-ɡən]|[-ɡŋ̍]|lang=de}}
* {{IPA|/mɔrŋ/|/mɔrjən/|lang=de}} {{q|colloquial variants}}
* {{audio|De-Morgen.ogg|audio|lang=de}}

===Etymology 1===
From {{inh|de|gmh|morgen}}, from {{inh|de|goh|morgan}}, from {{inh|de|gem-pro|*murganaz}}, from {{der|de|ine-pro|*merkʷ-||to blink, twinkle}}. Compare {{cog|nds|Morgen}}, {{cog|nl|morgen}}, {{cog|fy|moarn}}, {{cog|en|morn}}, {{m|en|morrow}}, {{cog|da|morgen}}, {{cog|sv|morgon}}.

====Noun====
{{de-noun|m|Morgens|Morgen|pl2=Morgende}}

# {{l|en|morning}}
# {{lb|de|agriculture|dated}} {{l|en|morgen}} {{gloss|measure of land, now only used informally, metrified as one quarter of a [[hectare]]}}
# {{lb|de|archaic|poetic}} {{l|en|east}}
#: {{ux|de|gen '''Morgen''' gehen|walk in the direction where the sun rises}}

=====Usage notes=====
* The normal plural is unchanged {{m|de||Morgen}}. The dialectal plural {{m|de|Morgende}} is formed under the influence of {{m|de|Abende|t=evenings}}. It is rather common colloquially but hardly ever used in literary German.
* {{m|de||Morgen}} includes the whole time of day between sunrise and noon, though the time roughly between 9 a.m. and noon is often specified as {{m|de|Vormittag}}.

